==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|lecherous}}, {{m|enm|licherous}}, from {{der|en|fro|*lecherous}} (attested in {{cog|fro|lecherousement||lecherously}}), from {{der|en|fro|lecherie}}, {{m|fro|licherie||gluttony, sensuality, lewdness, lechery}}, from {{der|en|fro|lecher}}, {{m|fro|lechier}}, {{m|fro|lekier}}, {{m|fro|lescher||to lick, live in gluttony or sensuality}}, from Old {{der|en|frk|*lekkon|*lekkōn|to lick}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*likkōną||to lick}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-||to lick}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|lecher|ous}}. More at {{m|en|lick}}.

